#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "Three conventions follow from the international definitions:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Parity indices are adjusted.** The ratio of one group to another is folded so that it's symmetrical around 1. If the ratio is above 1, it becomes 2 minus its inverse. Publications say which form they use."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Completion from administrative data is a proxy.** The SDG completion rate is defined over a cohort above the intended age, and it's measured mainly through household surveys. So a completion figure from an EMIS is labelled as a proxy."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Out-of-school counts need every level.** A learner enrolled at any level is in school. If the learner registry doesn't cover all levels, the out-of-school rate comes out too high."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "Worked example: gross enrolment ratio"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "The gross enrolment ratio for a level is the total enrolment in that level, whatever the learners' ages, as a percentage of the population of official school age for that level. Here's how it moves through the platform."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Gold stores counts** as at the census reference date. It holds the number of learners enrolled in each level, by area and sex, with levels mapped to ISCED 2011 ([CAP-TRANSFORMATION.5]{1}, [CAP-REFERENCE.4]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**The denominator is reference data.** It's the population of official school age by area, sex and single year of age, with its source and vintage ([CAP-SEMANTICS.5]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**The semantic layer defines the ratio once,** with its metadata and the edition of the definition it follows ([CAP-SEMANTICS]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**The snapshot is locked** when the census completeness gate reads CLEAR for the area ([CAP-COLLECTION.4]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**Disclosure control is applied,** and then the figure is published with a permanent identifier and its metadata ([CAP-PUBLICATION]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "**A revision is a new version.** Whether it's a late correction or a new population estimate, it creates a new version of the snapshot and of the published table, and the earlier version stays readable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/domain/indicators.md
msgid "Because the ratio is derived from counts and a versioned denominator, one definition gives you both the national figure and every area's figure. And when the population estimate changes, you see it as a new version, not as a silent shift. Don't be surprised if the ratio goes above 100 per cent: that's expected when learners outside the official age are enrolled."
msgstr ""
